(852553, 95362, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is stretching it for me. It took me a couple of moments to figure out it was an outline of the US. Someone else will probably think it is brilliant. I don''t really see an outline map as a miniature, at any rate. <br/> <br/>"Compose and photograph something "miniature" in such a way that it conveys to the viewer that the subject of your photo is a tinier version of something that is normally larger."</td>', 'This is stretching it for me. It took me a couple of moments to figure out it was an outline of the US. Someone else will probably think it is brilliant. I don''t really see an outline map as a miniature, at any rate.  "Compose and photograph something "miniature" in such a way that it conveys to the viewer that the subject of your photo is a tinier version of something that is normally larger."', '2004-08-10 13:41:53.000000', NULL, 1),
