(853145, 95664, 16488, '<td valign="top">Ahhh...know where you were!  I was here too, same week, but only down below. (don''t see that you got me in the pic)  Lovely place on earth, no?  What a roar it made in this unusually wet July!!!  This is a great capture. <br/> <br/>I know the answer to the question your title poses...so I don''t quite see it as answering my interpretation of the challenge.   Perhaps a polarizing filter would have minimized the flare on the highlights in the mist and (not surprisingly) dull sky above the falls?<br/> <br/>Hope you''re "local"!  It''d be nice to meet another dpc''r whose been to Taughannock Falls !</td>', 'Ahhh...know where you were!  I was here too, same week, but only down below. (don''t see that you got me in the pic)  Lovely place on earth, no?  What a roar it made in this unusually wet July!!!  This is a great capture.  I know the answer to the question your title poses...so I don''t quite see it as answering my interpretation of the challenge.   Perhaps a polarizing filter would have minimized the flare on the highlights in the mist and (not surprisingly) dull sky above the falls? Hope you''re "local"!  It''d be nice to meet another dpc''r whose been to Taughannock Falls !', '2004-08-10 22:21:32.000000', NULL, 1),
