(855248, 95562, 22484, '<td valign="top">Thanks all of you. Many many thanks.<br/> <br/>It is very nice and great for me because RESPECTED "STRANGEGHOST" and "GRAPHICFUNK" liked my shot. Thanks<br/> <br/>MANISH<br/></td>', 'Thanks all of you. Many many thanks. It is very nice and great for me because RESPECTED "STRANGEGHOST" and "GRAPHICFUNK" liked my shot. Thanks MANISH', '2004-08-11 16:08:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(855409, 95161, 24413, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by downward_spiral:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent idea, reasonable composition, but the lighting is harsh and nasty. Try using natural light next time, or perhaps a lamp/flashlight and a tripod.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree about the light.  It was a lucky shot.  My macaw doesn''t stay still for long.  I tried to duplicate the shot in different lighting but couldn''t.  I still felt it was worth entering because of the humor factor.  I feel pretty good about how it scored.  I think most everyone appreciated the humor in it.</td>', 'Originally posted by downward_spiral: Excellent idea, reasonable composition, but the lighting is harsh and nasty. Try using natural light next time, or perhaps a lamp/flashlight and a tripod.  I agree about the light.  It was a lucky shot.  My macaw doesn''t stay still for long.  I tried to duplicate the shot in different lighting but couldn''t.  I still felt it was worth entering because of the humor factor.  I feel pretty good about how it scored.  I think most everyone appreciated the humor in it.', '2004-08-11 17:21:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(855539, 95590, 22538, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everybody.<br/> <br/>I did try indeed to squeeze more into the shot than the miniature object itself and I am glad to see the message getting through. The setup was illuminated from two light sources, a red one from the left and a white one from the front. The red supplemented the light available from the two LEDs on top of the truck and added an air of urgency to the composition, while the white one brought out some detail in the front. The whole thing was finally sprayed with water. The picture is straight from the camera, after some sharpening.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Armin</td>', 'Thanks to everybody. I did try indeed to squeeze more into the shot than the miniature object itself and I am glad to see the message getting through. The setup was illuminated from two light sources, a red one from the left and a white one from the front. The red supplemented the light available from the two LEDs on top of the truck and added an air of urgency to the composition, while the white one brought out some detail in the front. The whole thing was finally sprayed with water. The picture is straight from the camera, after some sharpening. Cheers Armin', '2004-08-11 18:18:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(855585, 94351, 14812, '<td valign="top">What an original set-up. You''re on a roll with the ribbons, Daniel. Good work!</td>', 'What an original set-up. You''re on a roll with the ribbons, Daniel. Good work!', '2004-08-11 18:38:58.000000', NULL, 0),
